  ],
  "notes": "To convince someone through reasoning, explanation, or repeated appeal. The person being persuaded is marked with を. Unlike {命令|めいれい}する (to order), {説得|せっとく}する implies patient reasoning rather than authority.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {説得|せっとく}に{応|おう}じる: to yield to persuasion\n- {説得力|せっとくりょく}がある: to be persuasive; to have persuasive power\n- {説得|せっとく}を{試|こころ}みる: to attempt to persuade\n- {粘|ねば}り{強|づよ}く{説得|せっとく}する: to persistently persuade\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {納得|なっとく}させる: to make someone understand — focuses on the other person's comprehension and acceptance\n- {口説|くど}く: to coax; to woo — more informal, can imply romantic persuasion\n- {勧|すす}める: to recommend — softer, suggesting rather than arguing",
